86119855 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186408165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119855 #edb/ref 1039 "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119855 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186119670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119855 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120044 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120044 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120044 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120044 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120044 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120044 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120044 #edb/ref 1045 "The Column Space of a Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120044 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186120680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120044 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120044 #edb/ref 1050 1020.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120044 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "4f1a5ecd-cb6d-546d-a554-9b94e41a336a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120397 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186118496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120397 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35567" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120397 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120397 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ -15 \\\\ k+5\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120397 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "573bc22a-fac9-5364-8084-060fccb61060" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120397 #edb/ref 1074 "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 & 14 \\\\ -2 & -11 & -15 \\\\ 1 & 6 & k+5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ -2 & -11 & -15 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -3k-1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+10{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 17k-51\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=k+5 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2k-5 \\\\ 0=17k-51.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=17k-51,$ which means that $k=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120515 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120515 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74080" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120515 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120515 #edb/ref 1071 "The matrix $E$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{e}_{1}+{x}_{2}{e}_{2}+{x}_{3}{e}_{3}+{x}_{4}{e}_{4},$ and ${e}_{1}$, ${e}_{2}$, ${e}_{3}$, and ${e}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120515 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0554a363-6902-58e6-8a93-41a3bab0a0ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120515 #edb/ref 1074 "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\text{ }0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=2 \\\\ 0=-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-1.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120680 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120680 #edb/ref 1061 17489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120680 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e2b22098-86e0-53ea-bbc9-fc31b60b4152" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120680 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120681 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120681 #edb/ref 1061 17491 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120681 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "415a39b4-7da9-55ac-afde-f8932b3c0813" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120681 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120682 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120682 #edb/ref 1061 17493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120682 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "65ce55e4-127b-59e8-96ab-fabcdc24aef9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120682 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120683 #edb/ref 1061 17494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120683 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4b1277a3-a28d-5ae0-951f-c3f5b643aec1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120683 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120749 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120749 #edb/ref 1061 23239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120749 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b98e9e59-d7cc-545a-8c21-fb820acf8430" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120749 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121037 #edb/ref 1064 "The **column space** of a matrix $A$ is denoted $\\text{Col}(A)$ and is the span of the columns of $A$ (i.e., the set of all possible linear combinations of columns of $A$). For example, consider the matrix\n\n![](images/6c/6c03ab3dfd7b75c9a89defe102f33946da200fb88d26139e54c889a90467068a.svg)\nwhere we denote its columns by $\\color{red}\\mathbf{a}_1$ and ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{a}_2},$ respectively. The column space of this matrix is given by\n![](images/5f/5faad23bc77f821d42223beaca06364e38c7f0ba8a4869cb138e0e923e90b8f7.svg)\n\nNow, suppose we would like to determine whether the vector ![](images/45/45349edee356334c54ad85a6d60757a6a7833a392962086815a2436446e323dc.svg) lies in $\\textrm{Col}(A).$ In other words, we need to check if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ {\\color{red}\\mathbf{a}_1}, {\\color{blue}\\mathbf{a}_2} \\}.$ So, we need to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ can be written as some linear combination of $\\color{red}\\mathbf{a}_1$ and ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{a}_2}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equation above can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =b \\\\ {{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{x}} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{b}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation is equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$ To solve the equation, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ -7{x}_{2}=-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2=1.$ Substituting into the first equation, we get $x_1=-1.$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Col}(A).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of $\\color{red}\\mathbf{a}_1$ and ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{a}_2}\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/a3/a3965a53b3b3cfda2e11c4a68ba882631dc2763f32de67de30b4751aca76f2e5.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121037 #edb/ref 1065 3201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121037 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f65da145-207a-50c6-b59e-8756d247cc71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121037 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121038 #edb/ref 1064 "The column space is defined for matrices of *any* dimensions. In general, if ${\\color{black}\\mathbf{a}_1}, {\\color{black}\\mathbf{a}_2}, \\ldots, {\\color{black}\\mathbf{a}_n}$ are the columns of a matrix $A,$ that is to say,\n![](images/d9/d9d3fd7384b4375895d234c22c9d81f30358439f7e04ee8db055de9d5d7f1174.svg)\nthen $\\textrm{Col}(A) = \\textrm{Span} \\{ {\\color{black}\\mathbf{a}_1}, {\\color{black}\\mathbf{a}_2}, \\ldots, {\\color{black}\\mathbf{a}_n} \\}.$\n\nThe column space satisfies the following properties:\n\n- If $A$ is an ${\\color{blue}m}\\times n$ matrix, then $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ is a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^{\\color{blue}m}.$ This is because each column has ${\\color{blue}m}$ entries.\n\n- $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Col}(A)$ if and only if the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent (has a solution).\n\n- If the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is inconsistent (has no solution), then $\\mathbf{b}\\not\\in\\textrm{Col}(A).$\n\nThese hold for any $m\\times n$ matrix, and the matrix does not necessarily have to be square." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121038 #edb/ref 1065 3203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121038 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f33b7df2-b0c3-5b23-b26b-50509cefd3a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121038 #edb/ref 1067 "Properties of the Column Space of a Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244501 #edb/ref 1080 "-32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244501 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244501 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "145aaf0d-c740-5655-ae4b-ab7ab839b1d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244793 #edb/ref 1080 "40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244793 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244793 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3645011b-7dde-5f85-8688-666dc335211c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244911 #edb/ref 1080 "-21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244911 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244911 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "44437890-b323-5fd5-97ac-226cbb6e05ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246164 #edb/ref 1080 "-31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246164 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246164 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cf93de62-0950-5d23-bca5-5947fd12768b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246324 #edb/ref 1080 "-23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246324 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246324 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e1ef9d00-cd89-59a6-b58c-1a2654314dc9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246855 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186244501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246855 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186244793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246855 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186244911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246855 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186246164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246855 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186246324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246855 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246855 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246855 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186244911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246855 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "aa5a0518-d9be-57b6-b478-a86c9d9b1ec7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247190 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247190 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110979" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247190 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247190 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ k \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247190 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fc664822-35fb-5c04-9e53-89dd85c50706" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247190 #edb/ref 1074 "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ -5 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 6 & 42\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 42+2k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=k \\\\ 0=42+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=42+2k,$ which means that $k=-21.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315122 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315122 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045